(>> 3.4 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: Contrast all four C storage classes \(auto, register, static, extern\) across) Tj
T*
(storage location, default initial value, scope, and lifetime.) Tj
T*
(Answer: \(1\) auto: Storage: RAM \(Stack\); Default Value: Garbage; Scope: Local to) Tj
T*
(declaring block; Lifetime: Duration of block execution. \(2\) register: Storage: CPU core) Tj
T*
(register; Default Value: Garbage; Scope: Local to block; Lifetime: Duration of block) Tj
T*
(execution; Cannot take address \(&\). \(3\) static: Storage: RAM \(Data/BSS segment\); Default) Tj
T*
(Value: Zero \(0\); Scope: Local to block \(or file scope if global\); Lifetime: Entire) Tj
T*
(program execution lifetime; retains values between function invocations. \(4\) extern:) Tj
T*
(Storage: RAM \(Data/BSS segment\); Default Value: Zero \(0\); Scope: Global \(accessible) Tj
T*
(across multiple project files\); Lifetime: Entire program execution lifetime.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain the mechanism of recursive function execution using the activation) Tj
T*
(record and call stack concept.) Tj
T*
(Answer: When a function is called, the runtime environment allocates an Activation) Tj
T*
(Record \(Stack Frame\) on top of the program's call stack. The frame contains: \(1\) Return) Tj
T*
(address, \(2\) Storage for actual arguments, \(3\) Storage for local variables, \(4\) Saved) Tj
T*
(machine registers. In recursion, each recursive invocation pushes a NEW, independent) Tj
T*
(stack frame onto the call stack. These frames accumulate during the winding phase. If) Tj
T*
(base case is absent or incorrect, stack memory exhausts, causing fatal Stack Overflow.) Tj
T*
(When base case is reached, function completes and returns value; its stack frame is) Tj
T*
(popped off, and control transfers back to caller frame. Unwinding phase continues until) Tj
T*
(initial caller receives final accumulated result.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
